      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was physician-confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
